    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d880">

                <pb facs="0794" n="787" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg787"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/11564: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Second Secretary of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Atcheson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-12-10T00:00:00+08:00">December 10,
                        1937—midnight</date>.<lb/>[Received December 10—3:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1032. International Committee requests that following be communicated as soon as
                    possible to Japanese Embassy: <pb facs="0795" n="788" xml:id="pg788"/>
                    <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“International Committee, Nanking, for sake of 200,000 civilians, seeks
                            prompt and favorable reply to yesterday’s telegram regarding armistice
                            and withdrawal of Chinese troops from walled city of Nanking. (Signed)
                            Rabe, Chairman”.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>2. Sent to Shanghai, repeated to Peiping, Hankow. Nanking please repeat to Tokyo
                    with request that Embassy there communicate to Foreign Office.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Atcheson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
